{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"records\":[{\"exampleId\":\"D161-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"d06970a2cc6eb334a2dbb18112be4118d0fd92fdc478dc9c4f402ac502e594d5\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 replaces finding a door with waking a wall; A5 replaces waking with listening, but B2 prompts no new mission.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2 with 'At doors' but repeats A1's mission; B4's nonresponse does cause A5's listening.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 questions failure and B4 reports silence, without establishing why B needs this expedition to succeed.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 changes the activity to listening, but adds little commitment beyond A3's knocking.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a map and wall, but no destination or practical reason to find the door.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'At doors' economically limits the admitted failure; A5 stays within the wall premise.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":65},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The treasure map ends at this solid wall. It secretly led us here to wake it. I'm knocking.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Nothing. And our torch is nearly out.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then we were sent to hear it in darkness. I'm putting the torch out.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I can only hear you breathing.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"That's it. The map was testing our breath control. I'm holding mine.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"Each failed operation reveals a supposedly concealed objective, which A immediately begins pursuing.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Optimistic reframing could celebrate failure without replacing the plan's intended goal.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 makes waking the wall the real mission, and A5 replaces that mission with listening through it.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"This alternative uses physical exploration and dwindling torchlight; alternative b uses a radio operator's increasingly impractical assignments.\",\"reason\":\"The revision gives B practical pressure and makes both failures redirect immediate action. Internal reread scores fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4: 90. B4 identifies breathing, causing A5 to declare and begin breath control.\",\"reservation\":\"The revised breath-control mission is a substantial irrational leap; sincerity must make it feel discovered rather than chosen for a joke.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D161-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"ec379d4ea3184b83da1a059b582570c42a26de098a2dc9049032d0cff475bfa8\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 recasts transmission as reception and A5 declares learning silence; A3 mostly salvages reception rather than changing goals.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's static becomes A3's rhythm transcription, and B4's stoppage becomes A5's recording of silence.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 supply equipment updates but reveal no personal duty, urgency or competing choice.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 makes the mission more abstract but 'Keep recording' barely changes the practical commitment.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a failed signal, but the sender, recipient and purpose remain unspecified.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'Write the rhythm' and A5's 'Keep recording' express the logic without explanation.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":73},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Base can't hear our ship's report. We were secretly sent to receive. I'm switching channels.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Only static. I need a forecast before my watch.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"That's applause. Our real mission is entertaining base. I'm singing the forecast.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Now they've switched off. You've lost our audience.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then this was rejection training. I'm handing you the microphone; refuse me a second verse.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A treats each failure as evidence of a different secret assignment and immediately performs that assignment.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Persistence would keep trying to deliver the original report through another method.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 abandons sending, and A5 claims that learning silence was the purpose instead.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a turns exploration failures into bodily tests that consume useful resources; b turns professional radio duties into performance and then recruits the colleague to administer personal rejection.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass and replaced the rejected troubleshooting sequence within the shipboard setting. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 4, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 88. A1, A3 and A5 announce distinct hidden goals and immediate actions. B2's static becomes A3's supposed applause, while the requested forecast supplies the song. B4's lost audience defeats entertainment and causes A5's rejection exercise. B2 has watch duties; A5 draws that colleague into a more personal task. The microphone and second verse keep the concise final demand attached to the failed performance.\",\"reservation\":\"A3's interpretation of static as applause is a substantial inference, and B4's account of base switching off is accepted as scene information. A must sincerely discover the assignments rather than knowingly invent excuses.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D162-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"03c972f97d3df0f7ea70e8450926ab49cb173222ce8d647d802785737003104d\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 invents elementary cloud anatomy to answer B2; A5 invents dampness as the locating rule only after B4 asks where.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2's objection triggers A3's anatomical exception; B4's location question triggers A5's ruler test.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 make B a pupil asking the required questions, with no independent reason to measure.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 provides a new rule but announces success without a new consequence or increased demand.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1's cloud measurement lacks an accessible setting; A5 assumes a ruler can become damp against the cloud.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'elementary cloud anatomy' efficiently performs authority; A5 keeps the joke tied to measurement.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":73},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Before we sell this bottled cloud, measure from its third elbow.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'm the new assistant. I can only find two.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Naturally. The third appears when addressed by its professional title. Say 'Professor.'\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Professor. It's raining inside the bottle.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Excellent. Those are its credentials. Count the drops; that gives us its sleeve size.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A projects complete expertise while supplying a fresh nonsensical rule precisely when a practical question requires one.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Random surreal description can name strange things without maintaining an expert's responsive authority.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 answers the elbow objection with anatomy, and A5 answers the location question with a dampness test.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"This version makes A a shop expert inducting an assistant; alternative b makes A an expert responding to a malfunctioning gravity control.\",\"reason\":\"A bottled-cloud shop is a new illustrative setting that makes measurement playable and gives B a role. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4: 90. B4's rain creates A5's credential and sizing rules.\",\"reservation\":\"The final sleeve-size rule is deliberately strange; its connection to the established elbows needs confident, practical delivery.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D162-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"c0e1528712ec15dc7d2c4fa2bb363d5623639df6f4a93d4100e4a1e3df96f428\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 defines polite turning after B2 asks how; A5 interprets the newly reported click as acceptance.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 supplies B2's missing procedure, and A5 specifically interprets B4's click at six.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 requests instruction and B4 reports a result, but B has no visible purpose beyond assisting A's demonstration.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 confirms success without expanding the rule's demand or consequence.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a playable dial but does not establish what the gravity adjustment is meant to accomplish.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's pauses and A5's accepting six maintain one compact logic of etiquette.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":76},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"To get your sofa off the ceiling, turn the gravity dial politely.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'm losing my deposit. How do I turn politely?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Pause at each number. They dislike being passed over.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Six clicked, but now the armchairs are rising.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Six has invited witnesses. Apologize to the whole suite; private apologies don't count once furniture assembles.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A supplies authoritative rules of strange etiquette as each new operational problem makes them necessary.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Expanding an impossible world's lore would emphasize history and wider consequences rather than improvised procedural mastery.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 invents the turning procedure in response to B2, and A5 gives B4's click an expert interpretation.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a uses supportive instruction of a novice; this version puts expertise under pressure from a tenant's deposit and multiplying floating furniture.\",\"reason\":\"The revision adds a concrete repair objective and replaces mere confirmation with a consequential new rule. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 92. B4's rising chairs require A5's public apology.\",\"reservation\":\"The final rule approaches broader worldbuilding, though its immediate use as a repair instruction keeps procedural mastery central.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D163-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"7cf7d6c30ec6c312d751a205f23ce604caf7a2fcbe98d88211b748ed755baa29\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 extends a flying chair into a table and A5 adds a hovering waiter, each justified through hospitality.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's sufficiency objection; B4's acceptance of the table enables A5's service requirement.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 tries to limit the project and B4 concedes, but B's resources or purpose remain unclear.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 expands the accepted flying table into a staffed airborne meal.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes flying furniture but not whether these speakers are buying, building or arranging it.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's hospitality distinction earns A5's practical concern about landing for soup.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":75},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"For my restaurant, your flying chair needs a flying table. Dinner should travel with the diner.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I can make the whole table circle the room.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Add a hovering waiter. Nobody should chase their soup.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The waiter can serve while flying upside down.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then commission gravity-proof soup. I won't make customers rotate between courses.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A answers each impossible proposal by committing to a still more impossible provision with a practical justification.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Generic escalation can add extravagant objects without answering B's particular strange offer.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 adds a hovering waiter because B4 has accepted the flying table, preserving the hospitality rationale.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"This version has a supplier actively offering greater capabilities; alternative b uses a host negotiating accommodation for an invisible guest.\",\"reason\":\"The revision establishes a restaurant purchase and gives B two genuine strange offers to heighten. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 5, specificity 4, brevity 4: 93. B4's inverted service directly requires A5's soup invention.\",\"reservation\":\"The restaurant is a new illustrative setting. Gravity-proof soup is clear comic logic, but the actor must prioritize customer comfort over celebrating the invention.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D163-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"0ebecf03498860a768c4c3d17c6ec04a232b04074aafea7aaeffb37e743826f7\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 enlarges the invisible guest premise, but B2's headcount objection and B4's question offer no further strange capability.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2 by positing companions; A5 answers B4's quantity question by reserving the room.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 protects the invitation count and B4 seeks workable seating instructions.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 commits the entire room to the possible entourage introduced in A1.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a guest and places but leaves the hosts' event and authority vague.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 is compact, but untouched plates cannot clearly establish how many invisible diners attended.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":67},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Your invisible guest is welcome at our wedding. I'll reserve places for invisible companions.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Her family can walk through walls. They tend to wander.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I'll rent a ballroom that follows them. Nobody should miss cake.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Our ballroom can split itself when guests wander apart.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then I'll order a cake that multiplies with it. Every room deserves the first slice.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A commits to a greater impossibility in direct response to each strange offer, explaining its value to the occasion.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Inventing unseen extra guests alone could be assumption-making without reciprocal escalation.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 justifies invisible companions through hospitality, but the lack of a new strange offer from B4 weakens the exact mechanism.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a commissions increasingly impossible restaurant service from an inventive supplier; b has wedding hosts accommodate wandering guests with a pursuing venue and multiplying hospitality.\",\"reason\":\"Replaced the rejected invisible-wall and future-song justifications while preserving the wedding, invisible guest and companions. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4: 90. A1 establishes wedding accommodation; B2's wall-crossing wanderers cause A3's following ballroom; B4's helpful room-splitting capability requires A5's multiplying cake. B contributes family knowledge and a venue capability; A5 increases the catering commitment for a specific reason.\",\"reservation\":\"B4 introduces ownership of a miraculous ballroom without an earlier venue role. The shared wedding-planning context supports it, but the relationship is less explicit than the restaurant commission.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D164-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"614507c2a1cfe75c946d05cf136a1169b78b206a1dca082ad4c3764aa465caf8\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 turns the cupboard error into cleanup convenience; A5 turns the attic error into stair-free blanket collection.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's garden destination makes A3's equipment useful, and B4's attic supplies A5's blankets.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 wants the garden and B4 keeps trying the door, though B's contribution remains mostly corrective.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats the useful-supplies tactic without increasing commitment to the unreliable door.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's wrong cupboard and B2's garden establish an immediately understandable impossible route.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'without stairs' identifies a precise benefit of the attic mistake.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":84},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Our garden door opens into the broom cupboard. Wonderful, we can take a brush for the picnic crumbs.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Now it's the attic. I'm carrying all the sandwiches.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Perfect. Grab the picnic blanket without climbing stairs.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Now it's the cellar. The sandwiches are getting warm.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Built-in refrigeration. Put them beside the wine; this door is catering.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A treats each malfunction of an impossible door as an unexpectedly useful feature of that same system.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Failure Reveals the Mission would replace the picnic objective with a newly claimed secret purpose.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 and A5 keep preparing for the garden visit while praising benefits of the wrong destinations.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"This alternative makes domestic wrong turns useful for a picnic; alternative b exploits reversed time to improve a missed meeting.\",\"reason\":\"The original narrowly misses acceptance because its progression stays level. Internal reread of the revision: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 92. B4's cellar and warm sandwiches jointly cause A5 to entrust food storage to the malfunction.\",\"reservation\":\"The revised destinations still use a repeated discovery pattern; increased reliance on the door supplies the heightening.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D164-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"819abf11d8e9e2d5001518bd356daa4203e100cfd22bb0c8fac1a93b40133f4c\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 and A3 present backward time as an advantage, but A5's paperwork benefit is difficult to specify.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's missed meeting; A5 does not explain how B4's missing invitation constitutes solved paperwork.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 correct the timeline without revealing a responsibility or desired next action.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 praises efficiency but adds no stronger use of the clock than A3's earlier arrival.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a backward clock and B2 a meeting, but the practical chronology remains hazy.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1's 'early for yesterday' is concise; A5's paperwork claim sounds more like a tag than an earned benefit.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":60},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The office clock is dragging us backward. Excellent, we can attend the meeting we missed.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Too far. I haven't received the invitation.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Extra preparation time. This clock understands workload.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Now it's before the booking. The boss wants my opinion: do we need this meeting?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Perfect. Tell her no. We've upgraded from attending on time to giving everyone their afternoon back.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A converts every damaging consequence of reversed time into another useful capability of the clock.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simple denial would ignore the lost invitation or employer rather than identify benefits arising from those losses.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 uses the missed meeting to propose earlier arrival, preserving an advantage tied to the impossible system.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a finds useful picnic supplies through domestic wrong turns; b uses successive scheduling failures to gain preparation time and then prevent an unnecessary meeting.\",\"reason\":\"Replaced the rejected vanished-employer negotiation with an available decision-maker in the existing office setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 92. B2's absent invitation causes A3's preparation benefit; B4 explicitly supplies the boss's request before booking, enabling A5's cancellation proposal. A5 expands a personal punctuality benefit into time saved for all attendees, and B4 gives B actual influence over the decision.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 assumes the meeting is dispensable without discussing its agenda. That assumption is A's optimistic judgment; B can still defend the meeting or refuse the proposed answer.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D165-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"031bef62d2310e8020de8382c8076aa7235f24cdfa8758d33598c2c10d3af7a8\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 accepts three heads while objecting to crumbs, but A5's concern follows genuine fire damage rather than an ordinary detail.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2 with napkin etiquette; A5's coaster does not clearly address B4's burning table.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 expresses disbelief and B4 reports danger, but neither turn establishes B's practical relationship to the guest.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 increases damage stakes, yet A remains similarly admonishing rather than increasingly alarmed about something ordinary.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's dragon, carpet and crumbs establish a clear domestic visit.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's three heads sharing one napkin is compact and follows A's household standards.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":61},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Your dragon can stay for tea. Please keep the biscuit crumbs off my carpet.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"His three heads breathe fire. Should I take him outside?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"He's fine here. Wait, three mouths? I need three napkins immediately.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"He brought his own. They're paper.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Paper? At my good table? Fetch the linen before the neighbors see.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A calmly accepts the impossible guest while ordinary housekeeping and etiquette provoke increasing alarm.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General fussiness could complain equally about dragon fire and table manners, losing the contrast in emotional response.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 explicitly accepts the three heads and objects to crumbs; A5 blurs that contrast by responding to a burning table.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"This version escalates social embarrassment during a guest visit; alternative b prioritizes protecting furniture during levitation.\",\"reason\":\"The revision separates calm acceptance of fire-breathing from alarm over ordinary napkins. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 92. B4's helpful paper napkins cause A5's stronger etiquette panic.\",\"reservation\":\"A5's concern is status-conscious as well as domestic; the growing alarm needs to remain sincere rather than knowingly absurd.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D165-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"5350a3836ce22950c687280c0758f76a74cba1f2f6e9f64693dbc9ecf05563b4\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 dismisses floating furniture and prioritizes the wet cup; A5 still puts water damage before lowering the table.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 incorporates B2's rising table as travelling water damage; A5 conditions B4's proposed rescue on removing the cup.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 offers a practical intervention, and A5 materially changes its order.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 increases caution but gives little audible increase in alarm compared with A1.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's wet cup and floating table give actors a clear domestic problem.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'every altitude' attaches the impossible movement directly to the ordinary water ring.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":81},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The table can float while we pack. That wet cup needs a mat.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It's at the ceiling. I'll pull it down.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Wait! You'll slide the cup across the polish. Get the stepladder.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll climb up. I've still got my muddy boots on.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Boots off! Socks too if they're damp. We are not adding footprints to that water ring.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A treats levitation as manageable while becoming more urgent about ordinary marks and moisture.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Underreaction to danger alone would omit the required growing alarm about mundane details.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 delays B4's rescue to protect the finish, but its restrained wording underplays the increasing alarm.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a escalates hospitality etiquette; this version turns B's helpful retrieval plan into increasingly urgent surface protection.\",\"reason\":\"Packing adds a modest illustrative context and the revision makes the emotional increase audible. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 92. B4's muddy boots cause A5's expanded demands about footwear and dampness.\",\"reservation\":\"The final footprints imply B may step onto the floating table; that intention is inferable but not explicitly stated.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D166-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"682068bbd9fe68a621c829b625413a443aa629b7ea59a722629c2c4b326dc4ee\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 prices the ladder loan in a shadow, and A5 rejects money because it cannot perform the shadow's function.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's need for the shadow with an early return; A5 directly answers B4's cash offer.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 needs to retain a personal resource and B4 proposes a credible alternative payment.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 reveals the price's purpose but does not meaningfully enlarge the bargain or deepen the commitment.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a ladder loan, a price and a Friday deadline.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's early-return solution is economical; A5's literal use for a shadow earns the cash refusal.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":87},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Borrow my ladder for one shadow until Friday.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I need my shadow at work.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Keep its office hours. I'll take its evenings.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Could you hold the ladder too? I'm afraid of heights.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"For that, leave me your fear of falling. I'll keep it until you're down; you can climb without it.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A makes an ordinary favor conditional on payment in an impossible personal resource and negotiates within that valuation.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"An arbitrary surreal demand would lack the sustained exchange terms and payment function.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 sets the shadow price, A3 adjusts the loan duration, and A5 explains why cash is not an equivalent resource.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a now negotiates a shadow's availability and prices an additional physical favor in the borrower's fear; b accommodates a temporal correction by letting payment mature overnight.\",\"reason\":\"The original firstPass remains unchanged, but the supplied rejection establishes that its last line only explains the initial price. Revised within the ladder-loan setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4: 92. B2's work requirement causes A3's evening-only payment; B4 requests another favor and reveals fear, causing A5 to charge that very fear. The additional bargain offers B an emotionally useful consequence while preserving impossible payment.\",\"reservation\":\"A5's temporary custody resembles a deposit more than a permanent fee. It still prices the added favor in an unmeasurable personal resource, but the lender's reason for wanting fear remains open.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D166-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"114d59670499b234ea3573ad220f362f20821dd8004d67a966236ddb8511892b\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 prices kettle repair in a spoonful of yesterday; A3 and A5 preserve time as the required tender.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's collection problem; B4's 'That's today' directly causes A5's overnight maturation.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 tries to pay and B4 identifies a genuine flaw in A's proposed payment method.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 turns the correction into a delayed-payment arrangement with its own maturation rule.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's broken kettle and spoonful price make the repair bargain immediately playable.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'currency to mature' resolves B4's temporal objection through the already established transaction.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":92},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I'll fix the kettle for a spoonful of yesterday.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"How do I give you yesterday?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Start with the five minutes you wasted this morning.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That's today.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then leave it overnight. I can wait for the currency to mature.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"A prices a practical repair in impossible temporal currency and keeps negotiating how that currency can be supplied.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Fluent in Nonsense also improvises rules, but here every rule serves collection of the favor's price.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 explicitly exchanges repair for yesterday, and A5's maturation rule keeps B's correction inside that bargain.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a refuses substitution because the shadow has a specific use; this alternative accommodates B by letting the currency mature.\",\"reason\":\"Retained unchanged after internal reread at 92. B4 identifies the exact temporal error that A5 solves, giving the closing wit a necessary cause.\",\"reservation\":\"A3 shifts from a spoonful to five minutes 